# Model boundary

Cursor owns the **full stack**: everything under `src/**` — simulation kernels
and tests (`src/sims/**`) and the frontend (`src/app/**`). Kernels and renderer
are refined together so GPU acceleration and numerics can be co-designed.

Cursor must **not** edit:

- `docs/INTERFACE.md` — the `SimKernel` TypeScript contract is Claude-owned.
- `essays/**`
- Root docs/config: `README.md`, `MODELS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`,
  `HANDOFF.md`, `START-PROMPT-*.md`, `package.json`, `package-lock.json`,
  `tsconfig*.json`, `.cursor/rules/**`.

If the `SimKernel` interface shape needs to change (new method/field, changed
signature), **stop and write the proposed change as a note** in your summary.
Do not edit `docs/INTERFACE.md`. Claude edits and commits the contract before
dependent work. Implementation behind the existing contract is fully yours.

See `MODELS.md` and `AGENTS.md` for rationale.
